  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "kind": "equation",
  "id": "eq-model-sr-mirror-frequency",
  "paper": "special-relativity",
  "argument": "arg-sr-moving-mirror",
  "title": "Light reflected from a moving mirror",
  "spoken": "The reflected frequency ratio is one minus twice v over c cosine phi plus v over c squared, divided by one minus v over c squared.",
  "explanation": "Transform into the mirror's rest system, reflect there, and transform back. At normal incidence and v = 0.6c, receding, the reflected frequency is a quarter of the incident one.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The moving system moves along x at speed v relative to the stationary system, with |v| < c. Modern teaching notation: gamma is the paper's beta, c its V.",
    "A plane mirror at rest in the moving system, facing the incoming light; phi is the angle of incidence in the stationary system.",
    "The light reaches the mirror. For some angles and directions of motion it never does, and then there is no reflection to describe."
  ],
